# Ownership by team (ADR A, decision 10; the registry is osp/teams.yaml in
# build-kit), per the specification's stewardship and canonical-home rules
# (docs/SPECIFICATION.md in open-science-pillars/marketplace). The tools,
# gates and releases are the foundation team's; each bundle is its
# stewards'. One person occupies every team today; a provider person who
# takes the steward rung joins the bundle's team (the steward playbook),
# never by an edit here. A consulted provider's confirmation is recorded
# on the concept by the steward and needs no entry here.
* @open-science-pillars/foundation-maintainers

# The PO.DAAC bundle.
/knowledge/podaac/  @open-science-pillars/podaac-stewards

# The ESDIS cross-archive requirements bundle; ASSET members who take the
# steward rung join the team, their names landing with their first
# verified events, never before.
/knowledge/esdis/   @open-science-pillars/esdis-stewards
/knowledge/nsidc/   @open-science-pillars/nsidc-stewards

# Runtime projections (ADR B): the Claude package files are the Cowork
# projection of .osp/package.yaml and belong to the runtime maintainers.
/.claude-plugin/  @open-science-pillars/runtime-cowork-maintainers
/.mcp.json        @open-science-pillars/runtime-cowork-maintainers

# The Agent Plugins projection (plugin.json, mcp.json) and the release lock
# are rendered by build-kit from .osp/package.yaml and belong to the portable
# runtime maintainers; a hand edit fails the gate.
/plugin.json             @open-science-pillars/runtime-agent-plugins-maintainers
/mcp.json                @open-science-pillars/runtime-agent-plugins-maintainers
/.osp/release-lock.json  @open-science-pillars/runtime-agent-plugins-maintainers
